    "evidence": "REVISE q39 option b's internal misconception: omitting the cross term from (sqrt(x)-sqrt(y))^2 yields x+y=1, not the authored false relation x-y=1. With the author's chosen y=1 that omission produces x=0, not the displayed x=2. The separate derivation treating a squared difference as a difference of squares does reproduce (2,1), but the stated misconception does not. Keep the option and independent true set a,c; correct only the mismatch and obtain an affected review. No candidate was edited.",
